213   41AD              ; fall: A = the keys -> SPACE on a ledge starts a jump, the speed JUMP up;
214   41AD              ;       gravity adds GRAVITY to the speed, down at most MAXFALL, and the
215   41AD              ;       speed is added to y. Both are 8.8: the high byte whole lines, the
216   41AD              ;       low byte 256ths of a line. Going down, feet that reach the top of a
217   41AD              ;       ledge's cell stop there. Uses A, BC, DE, HL
218   41AD 2A 0B C1     fall:   ld hl, (vy)             ; 17  the speed, down positive
